+  // The sign of the non-floating-point 32-bit-per-component formats is applied
+  // to the guest data when it's converted to floating-point (see
+  // ConvertFixedPointGuestRange), so the signed and the unsigned versions have
+  // different contents even though the host format is the same for both.
